title Same speed, easy spin vs hard pedalling (level 3)

# The rider holds roughly 19 km/h. First an easy 50 rpm in a tall gear,
# then drops two gears and spins 90 rpm. A torque-sensor bike would help
# more when the rider works harder; this shows what a cadence-only PAS does.
at 1000 gear 2.6
at 1000 cadence 50 over 600
at 6000 gear 1.45
at 6000 cadence 90 over 400
at 11000 cadence 0

end 12000

# Baseline: harder, faster pedalling gets *less* assist ("keep current"
# tapers above 40 rpm), the opposite of a torque-sensor feel.
expect 5000 current == 14
expect 10000 current == 12
